WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.142 --> 00:00:04.857
- I actually did feel very guilty

00:00:04.857 --> 00:00:07.712
I had a lot of inner
conflict for many years

00:00:07.712 --> 00:00:10.670
when I first began the sport.

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:13.462
I felt that maybe I was
going against my religion

00:00:13.462 --> 00:00:17.045
and it really really
used to tear me apart.

00:00:17.961 --> 00:00:19.498
At the same time I loved the sport

00:00:19.498 --> 00:00:23.665
and I couldn't understand
how that could be wrong.

00:00:24.542 --> 00:00:27.357
I realized that I was
living a double life.

00:00:27.357 --> 00:00:31.072
One that I was a nice,
traditional girl at home,

00:00:31.072 --> 00:00:33.473
and the other where I succumb to the gym

00:00:33.473 --> 00:00:36.140
and that was another side of me.

00:00:42.838 --> 00:00:45.143
I remember the first time
I walked into the gym

00:00:45.143 --> 00:00:47.588
I was 18 years of age

00:00:47.588 --> 00:00:50.425
It was quite a male-dominated environment

00:00:50.425 --> 00:00:51.976
but none of that fazed me.

00:00:51.976 --> 00:00:55.976
All I wanted to do was
participate in the sport.

00:01:00.157 --> 00:01:02.026
Muay Thai originally was designed

00:01:02.026 --> 00:01:04.821
as a warfare art by the Thais.

00:01:04.821 --> 00:01:08.972
They used to use it to
defend their country.

00:01:08.972 --> 00:01:10.840
It is known as the art of eight limbs,

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:13.670
it's full-speed, full-pace, full-power,

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:15.801
and it's one of the
hardest sports in the world

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:18.468
so it can be quite intimidating.

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:22.167
(martial yells)

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:23.617
- To the right, Begum. To the right.

00:01:23.617 --> 00:01:27.610
- [Ruqsana] I actually began
my sport training with Bill.

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:30.789
He's actually become like
a father figure to me.

00:01:30.789 --> 00:01:33.457
He's took me under his wing.

00:01:33.457 --> 00:01:36.121
At the same time he puts on his coach hat,

00:01:36.121 --> 00:01:37.557
he means business.

00:01:37.557 --> 00:01:40.463
I can't come up with
excuses, I can't moan about

00:01:40.463 --> 00:01:42.873
that I'm in pain or I'm having a bad day.

00:01:42.873 --> 00:01:47.040
When you're in training
mode, you're in training.

00:01:53.543 --> 00:01:57.373
The fact that I come from a
traditional Muslim background

00:01:57.373 --> 00:02:01.540
is quite unusual to pursue
a sport such as Muay Thai.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:07.556
I was afraid that my family
might tell me sport, or them.

00:02:11.298 --> 00:02:14.253
I remember coming home one
day, and my father looked at me

00:02:14.253 --> 00:02:17.205
and he said to me "Why do
you walk like a boxer?"

00:02:17.205 --> 00:02:21.009
At that point I was so
frightened that the sport

00:02:21.009 --> 00:02:23.198
would be taken away from
me I ran up to my room,

00:02:23.198 --> 00:02:24.861
I had one trophy.

00:02:24.861 --> 00:02:27.722
I hid that, because I
thought that's the one key

00:02:27.722 --> 00:02:31.638
that gave it away that
I might be doing boxing.

00:02:31.638 --> 00:02:33.078
I decided to tell them,

00:02:33.078 --> 00:02:36.056
and I brought my father down
to the gym to reassure him

00:02:36.056 --> 00:02:39.175
that all I was doing was
exercising some discipline

00:02:39.175 --> 00:02:41.953
in my life rather than
being out on the street

00:02:41.953 --> 00:02:44.870
getting involved with
things that I shouldn't be.

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:48.022
Just knowing that they know
what I'm doing in my spare time,

00:02:48.022 --> 00:02:52.189
that's enough for me to
continue and make them proud.

00:02:53.134 --> 00:02:55.867
I don't want to walk away,
sitting in the changing room

00:02:55.867 --> 00:02:58.917
crying my eyes out, thinking
I could have done better

00:02:58.917 --> 00:03:03.084
or actually I had it in me to
win that fight but I gave up.

00:03:05.927 --> 00:03:07.652
(crowd cheers)

00:03:07.652 --> 00:03:11.152
- [Announcer] In the left corner, Ruqsana!

00:03:18.411 --> 00:03:19.775
- [Ruqsana] It's just me against her.

00:03:19.775 --> 00:03:22.459
Forget about her coaches,
forget about her supporters,

00:03:22.459 --> 00:03:24.240
it's all about what I can do

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:26.478
in these ten minutes of my life.

00:03:26.478 --> 00:03:27.747
- Round one

00:03:27.747 --> 00:03:28.663
(bell rings)

00:03:28.663 --> 00:03:31.246
(crowd cheers)

00:03:41.524 --> 00:03:43.078
- [Ruqsana] You don't
really have time for nerves

00:03:43.078 --> 00:03:45.652
all you're thinking about
is your next strike,

00:03:45.652 --> 00:03:47.747
your strategy: is it working, is it not,

00:03:47.747 --> 00:03:50.364
am I hurting my opponent,
am I winning the fight

00:03:50.364 --> 00:03:54.355
or do I need to change,
so it's very tactical.

00:03:54.355 --> 00:03:56.548
(crowd cheers)

00:03:56.548 --> 00:03:58.689
Obviously if you get
caught with a nasty shot

00:03:58.689 --> 00:04:00.989
you're trying to phase
that out very quickly

00:04:00.989 --> 00:04:03.018
and get back onto your game plan.

00:04:03.018 --> 00:04:05.018
(yells)

00:04:06.932 --> 00:04:08.471
(bell rings)

00:04:08.471 --> 00:04:11.054
(crowd cheers)

00:04:17.204 --> 00:04:21.083
- [Announcer] The winner
is, in the red corner,

00:04:21.083 --> 00:04:24.007
(crowd cheers)

00:04:24.007 --> 00:04:25.290
Ruqsana!

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:29.457
A round of applause, please
give it up for Susanna.

00:04:31.414 --> 00:04:34.392
(crowd cheers)

00:04:34.392 --> 00:04:36.013
- [Ruqsana] To win a
fight is one of the most

00:04:36.013 --> 00:04:37.975
amazing feeling in the world.

00:04:37.975 --> 00:04:41.736
it just reassures you
that all that hard work,

00:04:41.736 --> 00:04:44.869
all that sacrifice, everything
that everyone around you,

00:04:44.869 --> 00:04:47.049
the team around you, the nutritionists,

00:04:47.049 --> 00:04:50.016
your training partners,
all those nights training,

00:04:50.016 --> 00:04:54.183
sparring, going home with
bruises, all that is worthwhile.

00:05:00.763 --> 00:05:04.377
Talent alone is not enough,
it's all about sacrifice,

00:05:04.377 --> 00:05:06.960
it's all about being dedicated.

00:05:08.037 --> 00:05:11.537
And it's never the end, until you give up.

